"""Derive SkyyCooking/build_skyycooking_0.1.6.py from the SET pin build_skyycooking_0.1.5.py (itself generated by tools/cooking_0_1_5_patch.py):
rep(old, new) with asserted anchors, newline-agnostic (the line endings of 0.1.5 are kept). Edit THIS patch, never the generated build script.
Run: python tools/cooking_0_1_6_patch.py, then python SkyyCooking/build_skyycooking_0.1.6.py.

0.1.6 = INGREDIENT XP BY DIFFICULTY (lean round). Skyy 2026-10-05 (LOCKED): "Flour should go way down. The less it takes to craft, and the
earlier the items are to get, the less xp it should give you".
 - Until 0.1.5 every INGREDIENT craft (flour, dough, salt, spices, cheese, raw fish cleaning) paid 15% of its own direct raw inputs x 950:
   Flour 1,425 per craft - more than a Vegetable Skewer (1,050). 0.1.6 gives ingredients the dish table's difficulty idea at a far smaller
   scale (per mille of the craft's own direct raw inputs x 950):
     ING_BASE 15 + ING_STEP 15 per earlier crafting step in its chain (dough needs flour) + ING_KIND 5 per extra distinct input
     + ING_TIERW 15 per ingredient tier above 1 (the 0.1.5 Bazaar ladder: Milk T2 -> cheese)
   Flour 140 (13% of a Vegetable Skewer), every ingredient below the cheapest multi-step dish; the dish table is unchanged. Build asserts
   hold these rules; the route check proves no ingredient is a faster way to level than any dish, and the meat-pie route stays 25-30 h.
 - ONE-TIME UPDATE (new class CookIngMig, setup() right after CookTblMig.migrate, before CookCfg.load + CfgPub.start): CookTblMig's
   reviewed code with the ingredient keys - every xp.<ingredient> line still holding exactly its 0.1.5 default text gets the 0.1.6 value;
   anything else is kept and logged; the three 0.1.5 help lines of the xp block (byte-exact) are replaced 1:1; History copy verified
   first; one Undo-able change-log line per changed entry; run-once marker XP_ING_MARK above the xp block's comment run; every other
   byte and line ending kept.
"""
import os
ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
src = os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyCooking", "build_skyycooking_0.1.5.py")
dst = os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyCooking", "build_skyycooking_0.1.6.py")
raw = open(src, encoding="utf8", newline="").read()
CR, LF = chr(13), chr(10)
NL = CR + LF if (CR + LF) in raw else LF
s = raw.replace(CR + LF, LF)


def rep(old, new):
    global s
    n = s.count(old)
    assert n == 1, "anchor count %d: %s" % (n, old[:120])
    s = s.replace(old, new, 1)


